      "spam": false,
      "value": "@{58c6d558ff44e44ada717902|full_name}: A couple of ideas there... maybe users who have blocked the person who is being voted on automatically count as a \"yes\" vote since they have blocked the person? And a small premade list of reasons for the vote-kick might be helpful too, so the person who initiates the vote kick can select one of these, it gets displayed to others who are voting, and if the person is kicked, the reason why gets displayed to them too.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
